      "answer": " The API specifications folder is `/ULI-Xyne Final/Technical Documents/API Specs` (folder ID: `18aa30b5-d072-45c8-bda2-323247e88722`).\n\nBased on the relevant API specifications found, I can provide the token validity information:\n\n## Token Validity\n\nAccording to the **Authentication Service API specification**, the JWT token validity is:\n\n| Environment | Token Validity |\n|-------------|----------------|\n| **Sandbox** | **6 hours** |\n| **Production** | **6 hours** |\n\n### Content Citations:\n\nFrom the **Authentication and Authorization API Specification V1.2.1** (file: `API_AC001_Authentication Service_V1.2.1.pdf`):\n\n> \"Platform 'authentication' means the process where in every lender is required to obtain a unique access token based on OAuth2.0 from the Platform, which is **valid for 6 hours** and the same is used by the lenders for the subscribed API.\" [Kclf-tqo00u5f5ly22rdzrox7e9qq_5]\n\n> \"The JWT will remain **valid for 6 hours**.\" [Kclf-tqo00u5f5ly22rdzrox7e9qq_19]\n\n> \"Token validity in seconds. It will be **21600 seconds i.e., 6 hours** in actual response.\" [Kclf-tqo00u5f5ly22rdzrox7e9qq_19]\n\nThe authentication specification consistently states that tokens are valid for **6 hours in both Sandbox and Production environments**. This is confirmed across multiple API specification documents including Transliteration Service, LRS Master Data Service, and Account Aggregator Service, which all reference the same 6-hour token validity for both environments [Kclf-sw77fgtpo3mcmr5zjh70k99e_12], [Kclf-c1e3900q94htmnhpcs6wzsqi_11], [Kclf-nkcs8vdqhfgwgusm3woyhzcw_12].",
